course: dictionary
lesson: 15058
title: Revers: a coat word or a spelling clue?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A revers is a rare word from sewing and fashion. It is the part of a collar or cuff that is folded back, so the inside shows. «She turned up the revers of her coat to keep out the wind.» The fold is what matters here: the revers is the turned-back part, not the whole coat.
explain: Most pupils will never need this word, so do not worry if it is new. Look for the clue in the shape: a revers is folded back, like the lapel on a jacket.
explain: You may often see «revers» spelled wrongly. When you see it in your own writing or in a text, ask: did the writer mean «reverse»? Reverse means to go backwards, the opposite, or the back side. «Please reverse the car into the space.» Try your meaning in the sentence to check.
fact: A revers is the part of a collar or cuff that is turned back so the inside shows.
fact: A revers is like a lapel on a jacket. It is a rare fashion and sewing word.
fact: Often «revers» is a misspelling of «reverse».
fact: «Reverse» means to go backwards, the opposite, or the back side.
fact: Useful phrases with reverse: in reverse, reverse the car, reverse order.
exercise: «She turned up the revers of her coat to keep out the wind.» What is a revers? | A button that holds a belt | *The part of a collar or cuff that is turned back | A wet, grey day | A pocket sewn on the front of a skirt
exercise: Your friend writes, «Please revers the car into the space.» What word did she probably mean? | rivers | *reverse | revers
exercise: «Put the list in reverse order.» What does reverse mean here? | Very fast | *Backwards, the opposite way | Into a bag | Cold and wet
test: «He wore a grey jacket with a red thread along the revers.» Where is the revers? | On the shoe | *On the collar or cuff, folded back | Under the buttons | Inside the pocket
test: Which of these means to go backwards? | river | rebel | *reverse | revers
exam: Which is the correct spelling for a car going backwards? | revers | revearse | reverce | *reverse
